  "slug": "kitaev-charge-transfer-e280",
  "summary": "Recent preprints apply exact solvability to non-Hermitian, disordered and hyperbolic lattice models, probing exceptional spectra, fragmentation and localization.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is exact or analytically controlled analysis of lattice models whose spectra or localization depart from Hermitian, translation-invariant behavior. An exactly solvable non-Hermitian Kitaev chain with unequal pairing amplitudes shows an exceptional point where many-body energies collapse, together with Lifshitz criticality. Non-Hermitian fermionic chains with random imaginary gauge fields display erratic skin localization and density fragmentation into Fermi domains. A disordered spin-1 chain with an exact binary-tree Fock-space structure rigorously bounds spreading at strong disorder. The three-colored Kitaev model on finite hyperbolic periodic-boundary clusters is analyzed through ground-state flux sectors and two-vison gaps. The new element is the combination of exact solvability with diagnostics of exceptional spectra, fragmentation and localization across non-Hermitian, disordered and hyperbolic-geometry settings.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
